WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.157
Third Normal Form removes transitive dependencies
Even after separating

00:00:06.183 --> 00:00:09.907
appointment and service facts we should not keep
patient name and provider

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:14.025
specialty inside every appointment row if those
values are determined by patient

00:00:14.051 --> 00:00:19.654
or provider identifiers The appointment should store
the foreign keys that

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:25.592
identify the patient and provider Patient details
belong in patient

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:32.876
Provider details belong in provider A common memory
aid for 3NF

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.903
is that non-key facts should describe the key and
should not really

00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:41.420
depend on another non-key attribute The practical
benefit is easier

00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:47.041
maintenance If a provider's specialty changes we
update the provider record rather

00:00:47.054 --> 00:00:48.528
than many appointment rows
